WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.858
Here is how to install Frog Bot on Linux. One command does it, on any 64 bit Linux.

00:00:08.258 --> 00:00:15.242
First, open a terminal. On Ubuntu, press Control, Alt and T together.

00:00:15.642 --> 00:00:29.304
Go to the Frog Bot website, copy the Linux install command, paste it into the terminal, and press Enter. It may ask for your password once, to set up the browser security sandbox.

00:00:29.704 --> 00:00:36.373
Frog Bot opens on the sign in screen. The first time, click Create an account.

00:00:36.773 --> 00:00:46.966
Enter your name, your email, and a password of at least six characters. Then click Create account. Your team is private to your account.

00:00:47.366 --> 00:00:56.419
Next, paste your Claude or OpenAI API key, and click Start. Your key stays encrypted on your own computer.

00:00:56.819 --> 00:01:07.337
This is your team. Frog is your lead agent. Say hi, and tell it what you need, in plain words, like you would tell a coworker.

00:01:07.737 --> 00:01:18.160
Your name shows at the bottom left. Click it any time to change your picture, or to sign out. That is it. You are ready to go.

00:01:18.571 --> 00:01:24.994
Next time, open Frog Bot from your apps menu, or type frogbot in a terminal.
